mergency Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nOphthalmology\nUrgent Care\nPrevious Slide\nNext Slide\n24/7 Emergency and Specialty Pet Care Close to Home\nServing more than 16,000 patients a year, the MedVet Asheville team is a trusted partner in care for family veterinarians and pet lovers in Asheville, Buncombe County, and surrounding communities in North Carolina. We serve as an extension of your family veterinarian by providing advanced emergency and specialty pet care.\nOur 24-hour veterinary emergency care is available every day of the year to care for your pet when emergencies arise. When your pet is in critical condition, you can count on our expert team to deliver skillful, compassionate care to help your pet achieve the best possible outcome. If your pet is facing an emergency, you can come directly to our animal hospital – no appointment is needed.\nMedVet Asheville Caregivers\nSearch by Name\nFilter by Specialty\nAll Specialties\nEmergency Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nOphthalmology\nOur Hospital Leaders\nJacob G. Klos, DVM\nMedical Director\nKristin Hennessy, CVT\nHospital Director\nOur Doctors\nDayna Baxter\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nNora Collins\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nJacob Klos\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nCarmen Lindheimer\n, DVM, MS\nEmergency Medicine\nHaley G. Shaw\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nShayna Sosnowik\n, DVM, DACVO®\nOphthalmology\nAdam L. Stretch\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nCaroline Sullivan\n, DVM, MPH\nEmergency Medicine\nMatthew E. Tonero\n, DVM, Residency Trained in Veterinary Internal Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nSpencer Traynham\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nCasey Wesselman\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nPet Stories\n“They helped me through a heartbreakingly scary situation with my beloved but extremely stranger-shy blue heeler. The staff were wonderful during phone calls, registration, and our visit. My Diamond has always had stranger aggression and anxiety, making this terrifying situation even harder. I can’t thank the staff enough for Diamond’s wonderful care and quick treatment.”\nPrevious Story\nNext Story\nFinancing Options\nWe understand that planning for the cost of care is important. Special financing and payment arrangements are available for qualified pet owners through an independent company, CareCredit.\nLearn More\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nYouTube\nPartners\nVetRad\nVeterinary Eye Institute\nMedVet Suppliers\nLegal\nPrivacy Policy\nCA Privacy\nYour Privacy Choices\nTerms\nTransparency in Coverage\nTax Information",
